1. Display first name, last name and salary of employees whose salary is not in the range 10,000 to 15,000.
--> SELECT first_name, last_name, salary FROM employees WHERE salary NOT BETWEEN 10000 AND 15000;
Output:
+------------+-----------+--------+
| first_name | last_name | salary |
+------------+-----------+--------+
| Steven     | King      | 24000  |
| Lex        | De Haan   | 17000  |
| Alexander  | Hunold    | 9000   |
+------------+-----------+--------+

2. Display first name, last name and department ID of employees in departments 30 or 100, in ascending order.
--> SELECT first_name, last_name, department_id FROM employees WHERE department_id IN (30, 100) ORDER BY department_id ASC;
Output:
+------------+-----------+---------------+
| first_name | last_name | department_id |
+------------+-----------+---------------+
| Den        | Raphaely  | 30            |
| Alexander  | Khoo      | 30            |
| Nancy      | Greenberg | 100           |
+------------+-----------+---------------+

